{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","version": "2.1.0","runs": [{"tool": {"driver": {"name": "dependency-check","version": "9.2.0","informationUri": "https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/","rules": [{"id": "CVE-2022-23539","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - CVE-2022-23539 Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Versions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm. You are affected if you are using an algorithm and a key type other than a combination listed in the GitHub Security Advisory as unaffected. This issue has been fixed, please update to version 9.0.0. This version validates for asymmetric key type and algorithm combinations. Please refer to the above mentioned algorithm \/ key type combinations for the valid secure configuration. After updating to version 9.0.0, if you still intend to continue with signing or verifying tokens using invalid key type\/algorithm value combinations, you\u2019ll need to set the `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and\/or `verify()` functions."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 8.100000381469727,"security-severity": "8.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Versions of the package sanitize-html before 2.12.1 are vulnerable to Information Exposure when used on the backend and with the style attribute allowed, allowing enumeration of files in the system (including project dependencies). An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to gather details about the file system structure and dependencies of the targeted server."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.300000190734863,"security-severity": "5.300000190734863","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Affected versions of `sanitize-html` are vulnerable to cross-site scripting when allowedTags includes at least one `nonTextTag`.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n```js\nvar sanitizeHtml = require('sanitize-html');\n\nvar dirty = '!<textarea>&lt;\/textarea&gt;<svg\/onload=prompt`xs`&gt;<\/textarea>!';\nvar clean = sanitizeHtml(dirty, {\n    allowedTags: [ 'textarea' ]\n});\n\nconsole.log(clean);\n\n\/\/ !<textarea><\/textarea><svg\/onload=prompt`xs`><\/textarea>!\n```\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.11.4 or later."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2021-26539","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - CVE-2021-26539 Improper Input Validation vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.1 does not properly handle internationalized domain name (IDN) which could allow an attacker to bypass hostname whitelist validation set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.300000190734863,"security-severity": "5.300000190734863","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr","shortDescription": {"text": "critical severity - GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in a Command ('Command Injection') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/marsdb@0.6.11"},"fullDescription": {"text": "All versions of `marsdb` are vulnerable to Command Injection. In the `DocumentMatcher` class, selectors on `$where` clauses are passed to a Function constructor unsanitized. This allows attackers to run arbitrary commands in the system when the function is executed.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nNo fix is currently available. Consider using an alternative package until a fix is made available."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2015-9235","shortDescription": {"text": "critical severity - CVE-2015-9235 Improper Certificate Validation vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "jsonwebtoken Verification Bypass - NPM\n\nThe software does not validate, or incorrectly validates, a certificate."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 9.100000381469727,"security-severity": "9.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "CRITICAL","cvssv3_version": "_3_0","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "CVE-2022-23540","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - CVE-2022-23540 Improper Authentication vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "In versions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library, lack of algorithm definition in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification. Users are affected if you do not specify algorithms in the `jwt.verify()` function. This issue has been fixed, please update to version 9.0.0 which removes the default support for the none algorithm in the `jwt.verify()` method. There will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you don\u2019t need to allow for the `none` algorithm. If you need 'none' algorithm, you have to explicitly specify that in `jwt.verify()` options.\n"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 7.599999904632568,"security-severity": "7.599999904632568","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "CVE-2021-23771","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - CVE-2021-23771 Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/notevil@1.3.3"},"fullDescription": {"text": "This affects all versions of package notevil; all versions of package argencoders-notevil. It is vulnerable to Sandbox Escape leading to Prototype pollution. The package fails to restrict access to the main context, allowing an attacker to add or modify an object's prototype. **Note:** This vulnerability derives from an incomplete fix in [SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878](https:\/\/security.snyk.io\/vuln\/SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878)."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,"security-severity": "6.5","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/%40angular%2Fcore@9.0.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "A vulnerability was found in Angular up to 11.0.4\/11.1.0-next.2. It has been classified as problematic. Affected is the handling of comments. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. It is possible to launch the attack remotely but it might require an authentication first. Upgrading to version 10.2.5, 11.0.5 or 11.1.0-next.3 is advised to to address this issue."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.400000095367432,"security-severity": "5.400000095367432","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "CHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq Improperly Controlled Modification of Object Prototype Attributes ('Prototype Pollution') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/notevil@1.3.3"},"fullDescription": {"text": "This affects all versions of package notevil; all versions of package argencoders-notevil. It is vulnerable to Sandbox Escape leading to Prototype pollution. The package fails to restrict access to the main context, allowing an attacker to add or modify an object's prototype. **Note:** This vulnerability derives from an incomplete fix in [SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878](https:\/\/security.snyk.io\/vuln\/SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878). This package has been deprecated."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.5,"security-severity": "6.5","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Affected versions of `sanitize-html` do not sanitize input recursively, which may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary Javascript.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.4.3 or later."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.099999904632568,"security-severity": "6.099999904632568","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "CHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2016-1000237","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - CVE-2016-1000237 Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "sanitize-html Sanitization not applied recursively - NPM\n\nThe software does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes user-controllable input before it is placed in output that is used as a web page that is served to other users."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.300000190734863,"security-severity": "6.300000190734863","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_0","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "CVE-2022-25887","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - CVE-2022-25887 Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "The package sanitize-html before 2.7.1 are vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) due to insecure global regular expression replacement logic of HTML comment removal.\n\nSonatype's research suggests that this CVE's details differ from those defined at NVD. See https:\/\/ossindex.sonatype.org\/vulnerability\/CVE-2022-25887 for details"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,"security-severity": "7.5","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6","shortDescription": {"text": "critical severity - GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6 Improper Input Validation vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Versions 4.2.1 and earlier of `jsonwebtoken` are affected by a verification bypass vulnerability. This is a result of weak validation of the JWT algorithm type, occuring when an attacker is allowed to arbitrarily specify the JWT algorithm.\n\n\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 4.2.2 or later."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r Improper Input Validation vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.1 does not properly handle internationalized domain name (IDN) which could allow an attacker to bypass hostname whitelist validation set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.300000190734863,"security-severity": "5.300000190734863","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6 Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in pkg:npm\/request@2.88.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "The `request` package through 2.88.2 for Node.js and the `@cypress\/request` package prior to 3.0.0 allow a bypass of SSRF mitigations via an attacker-controller server that does a cross-protocol redirect (HTTP to HTTPS, or HTTPS to HTTP).\n\nNOTE: The `request` package is no longer supported by the maintainer."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.099999904632568,"security-severity": "6.099999904632568","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "CHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in pkg:npm\/express-jwt@0.1.3"},"fullDescription": {"text": "### Overview\nVersions before and including 5.3.3, we are not enforcing the **algorithms** entry to be specified in the configuration.\nWhen **algorithms** is not specified in the configuration, with the combination of jwks-rsa, it may lead to authorization bypass. \n\n### Am I affected?\nYou are affected by this vulnerability if all of the following conditions apply:\n\nYou are using express-jwt\nAND \nYou do not have **algorithms**  configured in your express-jwt configuration.\nAND\nYou are using libraries such as jwks-rsa as the **secret**. \n\n### How to fix that?\nSpecify **algorithms** in the express-jwt configuration. The following is an example of a proper configuration\n\n``` \nconst checkJwt = jwt({\n  secret: jwksRsa.expressJwtSecret({\n    rateLimit: true,\n    jwksRequestsPerMinute: 5,\n    jwksUri: `https:\/\/${DOMAIN}\/.well-known\/jwks.json`\n  }),\n  \/\/ Validate the audience and the issuer.\n  audience: process.env.AUDIENCE,\n  issuer: `https:\/\/${DOMAIN}\/`,\n  \/\/ restrict allowed algorithms\n  algorithms: ['RS256']\n}); \n```\n\n### Will this update impact my users?\nThe fix provided in patch will not affect your users if you specified the algorithms allowed. The patch now makes **algorithms** a required configuration. \n\n\n### Credit\nIST Group"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 7.699999809265137,"security-severity": "7.699999809265137","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "CHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6 Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "# Overview\n\nIn versions <=8.5.1 of jsonwebtoken library, lack of algorithm definition and a falsy secret or key in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification.\n\n# Am I affected?\nYou will be affected if all the following are true in the `jwt.verify()` function:\n- a token with no signature is received\n- no algorithms are specified \n- a falsy (e.g. null, false, undefined) secret or key is passed \n\n# How do I fix it?\n \nUpdate to version 9.0.0 which removes the default support for the none algorithm in the `jwt.verify()` method. \n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you don\u2019t need to allow for the `none` algorithm. If you need 'none' algorithm, you have to explicitly specify that in `jwt.verify()` options.\n"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.400000095367432,"security-severity": "6.400000095367432","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh vulnerability in pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "libxmljs2 is vulnerable to type confusion when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking a function on the result of attrs() that was called on a parsed node. This vulnerability might lead to denial of service (on both 32-bit systems and 64-bit systems), data leak, infinite loop and remote code execution (on 32-bit systems with the XML_PARSE_HUGE flag enabled). At the time of publication, there is no fix."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 8.100000381469727,"security-severity": "8.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2023-28155","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - CVE-2023-28155 Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability in pkg:npm\/request@2.88.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "The Request package through 2.88.1 for Node.js allows a bypass of SSRF mitigations via an attacker-controller server that does a cross-protocol redirect (HTTP to HTTPS, or HTTPS to HTTP). NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 6.099999904632568,"security-severity": "6.099999904632568","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "REQUIRED","cvssv3_scope": "CHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv vulnerability in pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking the `namespaces()` function (which invokes `XmlNode::get_local_namespaces()`) on a grand-child of a node that refers to an entity. This vulnerability can lead to denial of service and remote code execution."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 8.100000381469727,"security-severity": "8.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4 Improper Input Validation vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.2 does not properly validate the hostnames set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option when the \"allowIframeRelativeUrls\" is set to true, which allows attackers to bypass hostname whitelist for iframe element, related using an src value that starts with \"\/\\\\example.com\"."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.300000190734863,"security-severity": "5.300000190734863","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959 Improper Authentication vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "# Overview\n\nVersions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library can be misconfigured so that passing a poorly implemented key retrieval function (referring to the `secretOrPublicKey` argument from the [readme link](https:\/\/github.com\/auth0\/node-jsonwebtoken#jwtverifytoken-secretorpublickey-options-callback)) will result in incorrect verification of tokens. There is a possibility of using a different algorithm and key combination in verification  than the one that was used to sign the tokens. Specifically, tokens signed with an asymmetric public key could be verified with a symmetric HS256 algorithm. This can lead to successful validation of forged tokens. \n\n# Am I affected?\n\nYou will be affected if your application is supporting usage of both symmetric key and asymmetric key in jwt.verify() implementation with the same key retrieval function. \n\n# How do I fix it?\n \nUpdate to version 9.0.0.\n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere is no impact for end users"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 5.0,"security-severity": "5.0","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "LOW","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "LOW","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "MEDIUM","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2024-34394","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - CVE-2024-34394 Access of Resource Using Incompatible Type ('Type Confusion') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking the namespaces() function (which invokes XmlNode::get_local_namespaces()) on a grand-child of a node that refers to an entity. This vulnerability can lead to denial of service and remote code execution."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 8.100000381469727,"security-severity": "8.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr Inefficient Regular Expression Complexity vulnerability in pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"},"fullDescription": {"text": "The package sanitize-html before 2.7.1 are vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) due to insecure global regular expression replacement logic of HTML comment removal."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 7.5,"security-severity": "7.5","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2024-34393","shortDescription": {"text": "high severity - CVE-2024-34393 Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection') vulnerability in pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking a function on the result of attrs() that was called on a parsed node. This vulnerability might lead to denial of service (on both 32-bit systems and 64-bit systems), data leak, infinite loop and remote code execution (on 32-bit systems with the XML_PARSE_HUGE flag enabled)."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 8.100000381469727,"security-severity": "8.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "HIGH","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "HIGH","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}},{"id": "GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33","shortDescription": {"text": "medium severity - GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33 Use of a Broken or Risky Cryptographic Algorithm vulnerability in pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"},"fullDescription": {"text": "# Overview\n\nVersions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm. \n\n# Am I affected?\n\nYou are affected if you are using an algorithm and a key type other than the combinations mentioned below\n\n| Key type |  algorithm                                    |\n|----------|------------------------------------------|\n| ec           | ES256, ES384, ES512                      |\n| rsa          | RS256, RS384, RS512, PS256, PS384, PS512 |\n| rsa-pss  | PS256, PS384, PS512                      |\n\nAnd for Elliptic Curve algorithms:\n\n| `alg` | Curve      |\n|-------|------------|\n| ES256 | prime256v1 |\n| ES384 | secp384r1  |\n| ES512 | secp521r1  |\n\n# How do I fix it?\n\nUpdate to version 9.0.0. This version validates for asymmetric key type and algorithm combinations. Please refer to the above mentioned algorithm \/ key type combinations for the valid secure configuration. After updating to version 9.0.0, If you still intend to continue with signing or verifying tokens using invalid key type\/algorithm value combinations, you\u2019ll need to set the `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and\/or `verify()` functions.\n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you already use a valid secure combination of key type and algorithm. Otherwise,  use the  `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and `verify()` functions to continue usage of invalid key type\/algorithm combination in 9.0.0 for legacy compatibility. \n\n"},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "For more information see [GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33)\n\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"source": "NPM"}},{"id": "CVE-2020-15084","shortDescription": {"text": "critical severity - CVE-2020-15084 Incorrect Authorization vulnerability in pkg:npm\/express-jwt@0.1.3"},"fullDescription": {"text": "In express-jwt (NPM package) up and including version 5.3.3, the algorithms entry to be specified in the configuration is not being enforced. When algorithms is not specified in the configuration, with the combination of jwks-rsa, it may lead to authorization bypass. You are affected by this vulnerability if all of the following conditions apply: - You are using express-jwt - You do not have **algorithms** configured in your express-jwt configuration. - You are using libraries such as jwks-rsa as the **secret**. You can fix this by specifying **algorithms** in the express-jwt configuration. See linked GHSA for example. This is also fixed in version 6.0.0."},"help": {"text": "","markdown": "\n\nIf this is a false positive - consider using the HTML report to generate a suppression file. For more information see [How dependency-check works](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/internals.html), [How to read the HTML report](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/thereport.html), and [Suppressing false positives](https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/general/suppression.html)."},"properties": {"cvssv3_baseScore": 9.100000381469727,"security-severity": "9.100000381469727","cvssv3_attackVector": "NETWORK","cvssv3_attackComplexity": "LOW","cvssv3_privilegesRequired": "NONE","cvssv3_userInteraction": "NONE","cvssv3_scope": "UNCHANGED","cvssv3_confidentialityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_integrityImpact": "HIGH","cvssv3_availabilityImpact": "NONE","cvssv3_baseSeverity": "CRITICAL","cvssv3_version": "_3_1","source": "OSSINDEX"}}],"properties": {"disclaimer": "Dependency-Check is an open source tool performing a best effort analysis of 3rd party dependencies; false positives and false negatives may exist in the analysis performed by the tool. Use of the tool and the reporting provided constitutes acceptance for use in an AS IS condition, and there are NO warranties, implied or otherwise, with regard to the analysis or its use. Any use of the tool and the reporting provided is at the user's risk. In no event shall the copyright holder or OWASP be held liable for any damages whatsoever arising out of or in connection with the use of this tool, the analysis performed, or the resulting report.","nvd": "This product uses the NVD API but is not endorsed or certified by the NVD. This report contains data retrieved from the National Vulnerability Database: https://nvd.nist.gov","cisa": "This report may contain data retrieved from the CISA Known Exploited Vulnerability Catalog: https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog","npm": "This report may contain data retrieved from the the Github Advisory Database (via NPM Audit API): https://github.com/advisories/","retirejs": "This report may contain data retrieved from the RetireJS community: https://retirejs.github.io/retire.js/","ossindex": "This report may contain data retrieved from the Sonatype OSS Index: https://ossindex.sonatype.org","NVD API Last Checked": "2024-06-14T16:01:16Z","NVD API Last Modified": "2024-06-14T15:15:52Z"}}},"artifacts": [{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/.eslintrc.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "79f2249d5c5011c182a0251083ba067c","sha1": "f90d0c96bd4c9305a1ee7dca7cba1c6601d1076b","sha256": "1d355ae0449fc6c5068b43bb21b050523662442e2ae628501e91d19a9b4c988c"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/frontend\/.eslintrc.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "7d498005c3a84e5806c2eee29392b296","sha1": "683a0b9703f4f72770988b26bef1a4df2958eee0","sha256": "295cebaa7ac3bd231432ea2fc9d168cdbaf45443f13330b1713ca16e5c31464f"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/frontend\/.stylelintrc.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "494da5790c0d7a524ceb7f636395d9ca","sha1": "a47e0c40a5260f7ed57a942b3e2e9e89646b883a","sha256": "aa29ce548c7b5bc052fefa64bee29b625b5fcd03e093ea5ff30a737ff3b27640"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/frontend\/package-lock.json?@angular\/core"},"properties": {"id1": "pkg:npm\/%40angular%2Fcore@9.0.0"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/Gruntfile.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "3d2f23412beba58227e120c12ab70312","sha1": "f041f345dbe4185892955472ae1e663625c5c146","sha256": "a1a431a858587d3ee7645809360fa0b7476f1dc8f3c96c248f2a159fe768275b"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?express-jwt"},"properties": {"id2": "pkg:npm\/express-jwt@0.1.3"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/test\/files\/invalidTypeForClient.exe"},"hashes": {"md5": "2319ac34f4848755a639fd524038dfd3","sha1": "3082a2f97b22b4602e8d39083eef2ca0f7e54c4c","sha256": "c90232586b801f9558a76f2f963eccd831d9fe6775e4c8f1446b2331aa2132f2"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken"},"properties": {"id3": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?libxmljs2"},"properties": {"id4": "pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?marsdb"},"properties": {"id5": "pkg:npm\/marsdb@0.6.11"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?notevil"},"properties": {"id6": "pkg:npm\/notevil@1.3.3"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?request"},"properties": {"id7": "pkg:npm\/request@2.88.2"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html"},"properties": {"id8": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/views\/themes\/themes.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "7837164319aebacb17b13c3f99ddba88","sha1": "69a56706bc0a6b129b9f5dee99b1e914a993db81","sha256": "31559447ac4738eef09630a686209a92fd870da10ea5abb6d1238379e61a4161"},"properties": {}},{"location": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/frontend\/webpack.angular.js"},"hashes": {"md5": "90242640ec6a07ef6dea1d6089f692fc","sha1": "dc039030b7676690b9749a296bc21b8e18910d91","sha256": "c5f6a29270db8717c28c94577665514c4896e395dca8382e23372f38cbdd4d50"},"properties": {}}],"results": [ {"ruleId": "GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-c75v-2vq8-878f - A vulnerability was found in Angular up to 11.0.4\/11.1.0-next.2. It has been classified as problematic. Affected is the handling of comments. The manipulation leads to cross site scripting. It is possible to launch the attack remotely but it might require an authentication first. Upgrading to version 10.2.5, 11.0.5 or 11.1.0-next.3 is advised to to address this issue."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "a9bd0cb99573916e5d14fe1c52debe37"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/frontend\/package-lock.json?@angular\/core","index": 3 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/%40angular%2Fcore@9.0.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2020-15084","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2020-15084 - In express-jwt (NPM package) up and including version 5.3.3, the algorithms entry to be specified in the configuration is not being enforced. When algorithms is not specified in the configuration, with the combination of jwks-rsa, it may lead to authorization bypass. You are affected by this vulnerability if all of the following conditions apply: - You are using express-jwt - You do not have **algorithms** configured in your express-jwt configuration. - You are using libraries such as jwks-rsa as the **secret**. You can fix this by specifying **algorithms** in the express-jwt configuration. See linked GHSA for example. This is also fixed in version 6.0.0."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "ca9ff179066551a6c940dec0165d42d6"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?express-jwt","index": 5 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/express-jwt@0.1.3"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-6g6m-m6h5-w9gf - ### Overview\nVersions before and including 5.3.3, we are not enforcing the **algorithms** entry to be specified in the configuration.\nWhen **algorithms** is not specified in the configuration, with the combination of jwks-rsa, it may lead to authorization bypass. \n\n### Am I affected?\nYou are affected by this vulnerability if all of the following conditions apply:\n\nYou are using express-jwt\nAND \nYou do not have **algorithms**  configured in your express-jwt configuration.\nAND\nYou are using libraries such as jwks-rsa as the **secret**. \n\n### How to fix that?\nSpecify **algorithms** in the express-jwt configuration. The following is an example of a proper configuration\n\n``` \nconst checkJwt = jwt({\n  secret: jwksRsa.expressJwtSecret({\n    rateLimit: true,\n    jwksRequestsPerMinute: 5,\n    jwksUri: `https:\/\/${DOMAIN}\/.well-known\/jwks.json`\n  }),\n  \/\/ Validate the audience and the issuer.\n  audience: process.env.AUDIENCE,\n  issuer: `https:\/\/${DOMAIN}\/`,\n  \/\/ restrict allowed algorithms\n  algorithms: ['RS256']\n}); \n```\n\n### Will this update impact my users?\nThe fix provided in patch will not affect your users if you specified the algorithms allowed. The patch now makes **algorithms** a required configuration. \n\n\n### Credit\nIST Group"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "43eac6c2c4b8ce914aaf288b06919c03"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?express-jwt","index": 5 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/express-jwt@0.1.3"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2015-9235","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2015-9235 - jsonwebtoken Verification Bypass - NPM\n\nThe software does not validate, or incorrectly validates, a certificate."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "8aed2fb8e9f5db46905bd254e0031b98"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-c7hr-j4mj-j2w6 - Versions 4.2.1 and earlier of `jsonwebtoken` are affected by a verification bypass vulnerability. This is a result of weak validation of the JWT algorithm type, occuring when an attacker is allowed to arbitrarily specify the JWT algorithm.\n\n\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 4.2.2 or later."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "b844ee40690191936283b88d810f6d19"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2022-23539","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2022-23539 - Versions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm. You are affected if you are using an algorithm and a key type other than a combination listed in the GitHub Security Advisory as unaffected. This issue has been fixed, please update to version 9.0.0. This version validates for asymmetric key type and algorithm combinations. Please refer to the above mentioned algorithm \/ key type combinations for the valid secure configuration. After updating to version 9.0.0, if you still intend to continue with signing or verifying tokens using invalid key type\/algorithm value combinations, you\u2019ll need to set the `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and\/or `verify()` functions."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "0c48af10bf07f0cdf94af7dc5db69a41"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2022-23540","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2022-23540 - In versions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library, lack of algorithm definition in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification. Users are affected if you do not specify algorithms in the `jwt.verify()` function. This issue has been fixed, please update to version 9.0.0 which removes the default support for the none algorithm in the `jwt.verify()` method. There will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you don\u2019t need to allow for the `none` algorithm. If you need 'none' algorithm, you have to explicitly specify that in `jwt.verify()` options.\n"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "48e2b96a66d4fb82d738f37267a51cc1"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-qwph-4952-7xr6 - # Overview\n\nIn versions <=8.5.1 of jsonwebtoken library, lack of algorithm definition and a falsy secret or key in the `jwt.verify()` function can lead to signature validation bypass due to defaulting to the `none` algorithm for signature verification.\n\n# Am I affected?\nYou will be affected if all the following are true in the `jwt.verify()` function:\n- a token with no signature is received\n- no algorithms are specified \n- a falsy (e.g. null, false, undefined) secret or key is passed \n\n# How do I fix it?\n \nUpdate to version 9.0.0 which removes the default support for the none algorithm in the `jwt.verify()` method. \n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you don\u2019t need to allow for the `none` algorithm. If you need 'none' algorithm, you have to explicitly specify that in `jwt.verify()` options.\n"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "47b3ee890cc0c24536a42a2539f1f171"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-hjrf-2m68-5959 - # Overview\n\nVersions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library can be misconfigured so that passing a poorly implemented key retrieval function (referring to the `secretOrPublicKey` argument from the [readme link](https:\/\/github.com\/auth0\/node-jsonwebtoken#jwtverifytoken-secretorpublickey-options-callback)) will result in incorrect verification of tokens. There is a possibility of using a different algorithm and key combination in verification  than the one that was used to sign the tokens. Specifically, tokens signed with an asymmetric public key could be verified with a symmetric HS256 algorithm. This can lead to successful validation of forged tokens. \n\n# Am I affected?\n\nYou will be affected if your application is supporting usage of both symmetric key and asymmetric key in jwt.verify() implementation with the same key retrieval function. \n\n# How do I fix it?\n \nUpdate to version 9.0.0.\n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere is no impact for end users"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "60443e6a98aabb71beabc3f39c624d6f"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-8cf7-32gw-wr33 - # Overview\n\nVersions `<=8.5.1` of `jsonwebtoken` library could be misconfigured so that legacy, insecure key types are used for signature verification. For example, DSA keys could be used with the RS256 algorithm. \n\n# Am I affected?\n\nYou are affected if you are using an algorithm and a key type other than the combinations mentioned below\n\n| Key type |  algorithm                                    |\n|----------|------------------------------------------|\n| ec           | ES256, ES384, ES512                      |\n| rsa          | RS256, RS384, RS512, PS256, PS384, PS512 |\n| rsa-pss  | PS256, PS384, PS512                      |\n\nAnd for Elliptic Curve algorithms:\n\n| `alg` | Curve      |\n|-------|------------|\n| ES256 | prime256v1 |\n| ES384 | secp384r1  |\n| ES512 | secp521r1  |\n\n# How do I fix it?\n\nUpdate to version 9.0.0. This version validates for asymmetric key type and algorithm combinations. Please refer to the above mentioned algorithm \/ key type combinations for the valid secure configuration. After updating to version 9.0.0, If you still intend to continue with signing or verifying tokens using invalid key type\/algorithm value combinations, you\u2019ll need to set the `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and\/or `verify()` functions.\n\n# Will the fix impact my users?\n\nThere will be no impact, if you update to version 9.0.0 and you already use a valid secure combination of key type and algorithm. Otherwise,  use the  `allowInvalidAsymmetricKeyTypes` option  to `true` in the `sign()` and `verify()` functions to continue usage of invalid key type\/algorithm combination in 9.0.0 for legacy compatibility. \n\n"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "9106862e2f9a1311fb825f7ae842c913"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?jsonwebtoken","index": 7 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/jsonwebtoken@0.4.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2024-34393","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2024-34393 - libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking a function on the result of attrs() that was called on a parsed node. This vulnerability might lead to denial of service (on both 32-bit systems and 64-bit systems), data leak, infinite loop and remote code execution (on 32-bit systems with the XML_PARSE_HUGE flag enabled)."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "3f21df8bfb23309d50dd3a4a59df39ac"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?libxmljs2","index": 8 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2024-34394","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2024-34394 - libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking the namespaces() function (which invokes XmlNode::get_local_namespaces()) on a grand-child of a node that refers to an entity. This vulnerability can lead to denial of service and remote code execution."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "3f0a0f5e973b0367141d08a2050e5729"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?libxmljs2","index": 8 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-78h3-pg4x-j8cv - libxmljs2 is vulnerable to a type confusion vulnerability when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking the `namespaces()` function (which invokes `XmlNode::get_local_namespaces()`) on a grand-child of a node that refers to an entity. This vulnerability can lead to denial of service and remote code execution."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "1dd29ee49a201633b34ddef99c7c64f6"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?libxmljs2","index": 8 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-mjr4-7xg5-pfvh - libxmljs2 is vulnerable to type confusion when parsing a specially crafted XML while invoking a function on the result of attrs() that was called on a parsed node. This vulnerability might lead to denial of service (on both 32-bit systems and 64-bit systems), data leak, infinite loop and remote code execution (on 32-bit systems with the XML_PARSE_HUGE flag enabled). At the time of publication, there is no fix."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "d470894d69ea93002fd9e28556e35a52"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?libxmljs2","index": 8 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/libxmljs2@0.33.0"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-5mrr-rgp6-x4gr - All versions of `marsdb` are vulnerable to Command Injection. In the `DocumentMatcher` class, selectors on `$where` clauses are passed to a Function constructor unsanitized. This allows attackers to run arbitrary commands in the system when the function is executed.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nNo fix is currently available. Consider using an alternative package until a fix is made available."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "a70528cce7cd1883bd4748145da9b003"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?marsdb","index": 9 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/marsdb@0.6.11"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2021-23771","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2021-23771 - This affects all versions of package notevil; all versions of package argencoders-notevil. It is vulnerable to Sandbox Escape leading to Prototype pollution. The package fails to restrict access to the main context, allowing an attacker to add or modify an object's prototype. **Note:** This vulnerability derives from an incomplete fix in [SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878](https:\/\/security.snyk.io\/vuln\/SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878)."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "7d1790b33a64f13d01b5a0d87de85d7a"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?notevil","index": 10 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/notevil@1.3.3"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-8g4m-cjm2-96wq - This affects all versions of package notevil; all versions of package argencoders-notevil. It is vulnerable to Sandbox Escape leading to Prototype pollution. The package fails to restrict access to the main context, allowing an attacker to add or modify an object's prototype. **Note:** This vulnerability derives from an incomplete fix in [SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878](https:\/\/security.snyk.io\/vuln\/SNYK-JS-NOTEVIL-608878). This package has been deprecated."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "3d74859994d2d358008598bd5acb225e"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?notevil","index": 10 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/notevil@1.3.3"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2023-28155","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2023-28155 - The Request package through 2.88.1 for Node.js allows a bypass of SSRF mitigations via an attacker-controller server that does a cross-protocol redirect (HTTP to HTTPS, or HTTPS to HTTP). NOTE: This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "5e800fd260249938b5d5af3d2859826f"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?request","index": 11 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/request@2.88.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-p8p7-x288-28g6 - The `request` package through 2.88.2 for Node.js and the `@cypress\/request` package prior to 3.0.0 allow a bypass of SSRF mitigations via an attacker-controller server that does a cross-protocol redirect (HTTP to HTTPS, or HTTPS to HTTP).\n\nNOTE: The `request` package is no longer supported by the maintainer."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "1d98019aa9f072e1237c26d270d8f7e5"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?request","index": 11 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/request@2.88.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2022-25887","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2022-25887 - The package sanitize-html before 2.7.1 are vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) due to insecure global regular expression replacement logic of HTML comment removal.\n\nSonatype's research suggests that this CVE's details differ from those defined at NVD. See https:\/\/ossindex.sonatype.org\/vulnerability\/CVE-2022-25887 for details"},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "06203718d926b57f5ab762bb846e642d"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-cgfm-xwp7-2cvr - The package sanitize-html before 2.7.1 are vulnerable to Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) due to insecure global regular expression replacement logic of HTML comment removal."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "85c21c89fea8057d7a481ff53506c441"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2016-1000237","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2016-1000237 - sanitize-html Sanitization not applied recursively - NPM\n\nThe software does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes user-controllable input before it is placed in output that is used as a web page that is served to other users."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "7f872b4a9dc6ecdd3d22615d2348c42e"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-3j7m-hmh3-9jmp - Affected versions of `sanitize-html` do not sanitize input recursively, which may allow an attacker to execute arbitrary Javascript.\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.4.3 or later."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "b5f7494b2e713d6474511bad908aa936"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "CVE-2021-26539","level": "warning","message": {"text": "CVE-2021-26539 - Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.1 does not properly handle internationalized domain name (IDN) which could allow an attacker to bypass hostname whitelist validation set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "bdb3e76ff39c7f030e8b704a2b8bd2fd"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-mjxr-4v3x-q3m4 - Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.2 does not properly validate the hostnames set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option when the \"allowIframeRelativeUrls\" is set to true, which allows attackers to bypass hostname whitelist for iframe element, related using an src value that starts with \"\/\\\\example.com\"."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "e3cd04105d698106548d86a483fc44f1"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-rjqq-98f6-6j3r - Apostrophe Technologies sanitize-html before 2.3.1 does not properly handle internationalized domain name (IDN) which could allow an attacker to bypass hostname whitelist validation set by the \"allowedIframeHostnames\" option."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "c74952ea5607dbb5774e2068bd12be4d"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-rm97-x556-q36h - Versions of the package sanitize-html before 2.12.1 are vulnerable to Information Exposure when used on the backend and with the style attribute allowed, allowing enumeration of files in the system (including project dependencies). An attacker could exploit this vulnerability to gather details about the file system structure and dependencies of the targeted server."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "e6e6adcffeb2b62d8c7c349c6290a71f"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}, {"ruleId": "GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r","level": "warning","message": {"text": "GHSA-xc6g-ggrc-qq4r - Affected versions of `sanitize-html` are vulnerable to cross-site scripting when allowedTags includes at least one `nonTextTag`.\n\n## Proof of Concept\n\n```js\nvar sanitizeHtml = require('sanitize-html');\n\nvar dirty = '!<textarea>&lt;\/textarea&gt;<svg\/onload=prompt`xs`&gt;<\/textarea>!';\nvar clean = sanitizeHtml(dirty, {\n    allowedTags: [ 'textarea' ]\n});\n\nconsole.log(clean);\n\n\/\/ !<textarea><\/textarea><svg\/onload=prompt`xs`><\/textarea>!\n```\n\n\n## Recommendation\n\nUpdate to version 1.11.4 or later."},"partialFingerprints": {"vulnerabilityHash": "f647cdad524bb3d8e943bf5b7b674822"},"locations": [{"physicalLocation": {"artifactLocation": {"uri": "file://\/builds\/agilesec\/tbdpwl\/juice-shop\/package-lock.json?sanitize-html","index": 12 }},"logicalLocations": [{"fullyQualifiedName": "pkg:npm\/sanitize-html@1.4.2"}]}]}]}]}